 use the relationships between the roots and coefficients of the given cubic polynomial equation. The given equation is:\n\n\\[x^3 - 10x^2 + 55x - c = 0\\]\n\nLet the roots of this polynomial be \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\). By Vieta's formulas, we know the following relationships between the roots and coefficients of the polynomial:\n\n1. The sum of the roots \\(r + s + t = 10\\),\n2. The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time \\(rs + rt + st = 55\\),\n3. The product of the roots \\(rst = c\\).\n\nWe are also given that the product of two of the roots is \\(30\\). Without loss of generality, let’s assume \\(rs = 30\\).\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(c\\), which is the product of the roots \\(rst\\).\n\nFirst, we solve for \\(t\\) using the sum of the roots equation:\n\\[r + s + t = 10\\]\n\nSince \\(rs = 30\\), we can express \\(t\\) as:\n\\[t = 10 - (r + s)\\]\n\nNext, we use the sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time equation:\n\\[rs + rt + st = 55\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(rs = 30\\) and \\(t = 10 - (r + s)\\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[30 + r(10 - (r + s)) + s(10 - (r + s)) = 55\\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[30 + 10r - r^2 - rs + 10s - rs - s^2 = 55\\]\n\nSince \\(rs = 30\\), we substitute \\(rs\\) into the equation:\n\\[30 + 10r - r^2 - 30 + 10s - 30 - s^2 = 55\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[10r + 10s - r^2 - s^2 - 30 = 55\\]\n\nRearrange to isolate the quadratic terms:\n\\[10r + 10s - r^2 - s^2 = 85\\]\n\nFactor out the common term:\n\\[10(r + s) - (r^2 + s^2) = 85\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(r + s\\) and \\(r^2 + s^2\\). From \\(t = 10 - (r + s)\\), we know:\n\\[r + s = 10 - t\\]\n\nLet \\(u = r + s\\). Then:\n\\[t = 10 - u\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(u\\) into the equation:\n\\[10u - (r^2 + s^2) = 85\\]\n\nWe know \\(r^2 + s^2 = (r + s)^2 - 2rs\\):\n\\[r^2 + s^2 = u^2 - 2 \\cdot 30 = u^2 - 60\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(r^2 + s^2\\) into the equation:\n\\[10u - (u^2 - 60) = 85\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\\[10u - u^2 + 60 = 85\\]\n\nRearrange to form a quadratic equation:\n\\[u^2 - 10u + 25 = 0\\]\n\nSolve the quadratic equation:\n\\[(u - 5)^2 = 0\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[u = 5\\]\n\nSo, \\(r + s = 5\\) and \\(t = 10 - 5 = 5\\).\n\nFinally, we find \\(c\\) using the product of the roots:\n\\[c = rst = 30 \\cdot 5 = 150\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(c\\) is:\n\\[\\boxed{150}\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{150}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
